        "0.0": "The Blessed Lord said: I shall teach you again that supreme knowledge, the highest of all knowledge, knowing which all the sages have passed from here to supreme perfection.",
        "0.1": "Those who take refuge in this knowledge and attain a nature like mine are not born at creation, nor disturbed at dissolution.",
        "0.2": "My womb is the great Brahman (primal matter); in it I place the seed, and from that, Bhārata, all beings are born.",
        "0.3": "Whatever forms are born in any womb, son of Kuntī, the great Brahman is their womb and I am the seed-giving father.",
        "0.4": "Sattva, rajas and tamas — these guṇas born of Prakṛti bind the imperishable embodied one to the body, mighty-armed one.",
        "0.5": "Of these, sattva, being pure, is illuminating and free from affliction; it binds through attachment to happiness and to knowledge, sinless one.",
